00:32:08,720 --> 00:32:09,720
- [Mike] Huge Tanhead here.

772
00:32:09,720 --> 00:32:11,220
- This is Valmont.

773
00:32:11,230 --> 00:32:12,730
- [Ginko] Valmont?

774
00:32:12,730 --> 00:32:14,230
I have nothing to say to you.

775
00:32:14,230 --> 00:32:18,740
- I'm calling you, inspector,
on behalf of law and order.

776
00:32:20,230 --> 00:32:21,730
- Good.
- I love Jerry Orbach!

777
00:32:21,740 --> 00:32:26,740
- I would like us to make a
little bargain, inspector.

778
00:32:26,740 --> 00:32:28,750
- You know how I
bargain with your kind.

779
00:32:28,740 --> 00:32:30,240
First, I put you in cages.

780
00:32:30,240 --> 00:32:32,240
Then I teach you to
sing beautifully.

781
00:32:32,250 --> 00:32:34,250
For once, we've
got special powers.

782
00:32:34,250 --> 00:32:35,250
- [Servo] Zing.

783
00:32:35,250 --> 00:32:36,750
- By getting you Diabolik alive,

784
00:32:36,750 --> 00:32:38,760
and then you can arrest him.

785
00:32:38,750 --> 00:32:42,750
- [Ginko] Well, well, at
last you got the idea.

786
00:32:42,760 --> 00:32:46,760
(Mystery Science
Theater 3000 theme)

787
00:32:49,360 --> 00:32:52,360
- Joe, give me the tape
recording of the meeting.

788
00:32:52,370 --> 00:32:53,870
- [Servo] Our Promise
Keepers meeting.

789
00:32:53,870 --> 00:32:56,870
- We've taken a democratic vote.

790
00:32:56,870 --> 00:32:58,880
Five in favor of my plan.

791
00:32:59,870 --> 00:33:01,870
And three against it.

792
00:33:03,380 --> 00:33:05,380
(loud gunshots)

793
00:33:05,380 --> 00:33:06,380
- I will throw my vote!

794
00:33:06,380 --> 00:33:07,880
Don't shoot, please!

795
00:33:07,880 --> 00:33:09,390
- [Crow] I'm gonna put a
piece of my tongue in there.

796
00:33:09,380 --> 00:33:11,880
- DOn't shoot, don't shoot!

797
00:33:11,890 --> 00:33:14,890
- Since you said
please, I won't shoot.

798
00:33:18,890 --> 00:33:19,890
- Ahh!

799
00:33:19,890 --> 00:33:22,390
- [Mike] Extreme
organized crime!

800
00:33:23,400 --> 00:33:25,400
- [Valmont] Clean up.

801
00:33:27,400 --> 00:33:31,910
- [Servo] If Northwest flight
attendants had their way...

802
00:33:31,910 --> 00:33:32,910
- Oh, Ralph!

803
00:33:33,410 --> 00:33:34,910
How nice.

804
00:33:34,910 --> 00:33:35,910
- [Mike] Toni, get dressed.

805
00:33:35,910 --> 00:33:37,410
- Fresh air--
- Scram.

806
00:33:38,910 --> 00:33:39,910
- Sure.

807
00:33:43,420 --> 00:33:45,420
- Now it's unanimous.

808
00:33:45,420 --> 00:33:48,420
- [Servo] Cavernous
noses are the best.

809
00:33:51,930 --> 00:33:52,930
- So...

810
00:33:52,930 --> 00:33:53,930
- [Mike] Should
we watch Sounder?

811
00:33:53,930 --> 00:33:56,930
- These new emergency powers.

812
00:33:56,930 --> 00:33:59,940
Ginko is really
putting the heat on us.

813
00:33:59,930 --> 00:34:02,430
If we don't play ball with him,

814
00:34:02,440 --> 00:34:03,940
we all wind up behind bars.

815
00:34:03,940 --> 00:34:05,440
- [Crow] Or waiting tables.

816
00:34:05,440 --> 00:34:06,940
- So we play ball, but how?

817
00:34:06,940 --> 00:34:09,450
- We catch Diabolik for him.

818
00:34:09,440 --> 00:34:11,940
We got the know-how
that the cops don't.

819
00:34:11,950 --> 00:34:16,450
- No one's ever seen
Diabolik or his girl.

820
00:34:16,450 --> 00:34:19,460
No one's ever seen
them and lived.

821
00:34:19,450 --> 00:34:21,450
- So what?
(hoarse wheezing)

822
00:34:21,460 --> 00:34:22,960
We got connections.

823
00:34:22,960 --> 00:34:25,460
We all know squealers.

824
00:34:25,460 --> 00:34:27,960
If all of us work
together on this...

825
00:34:27,960 --> 00:34:29,470
- [Mike] We can wipe out litter.

826
00:34:29,460 --> 00:34:30,960
- So long, Diabolik.

827
00:34:33,470 --> 00:34:35,470
- [Crow] Just airing
out the little sizzler.

828
00:34:35,470 --> 00:34:37,970
(sensual music)

829
00:34:37,970 --> 00:34:39,980
- [Servo] Phyllis
Diller dropped by.

830
00:34:39,970 --> 00:34:43,470
(stifling sneeze)

831
00:34:43,480 --> 00:34:47,480
- [Mike] Plumber pulled
this out of the tub drain.

832
00:34:47,480 --> 00:34:49,990
♪ Dee dee dah

833
00:34:51,490 --> 00:34:53,490
- [Crow] Diabol-lick.

834
00:34:56,990 --> 00:34:58,490
- [Servo] Honey,
I'm out of cash.

835
00:34:58,490 --> 00:35:02,500
Wanna roll around in
some savings bonds?

836
00:35:02,500 --> 00:35:04,500
- You've been
asleep for 20 hours.

837
00:35:04,500 --> 00:35:05,500
- 20 hours?

838
00:35:07,000 --> 00:35:09,510
- I slipped you a sleeping pill.

839
00:35:09,500 --> 00:35:10,000
- Why?

840
00:35:10,000 --> 00:35:11,500
- [Crow] When you're asleep,

841
00:35:11,510 --> 00:35:14,010
you don't talk to
me or touch me.

842
00:35:15,510 --> 00:35:19,020
- When you're not planning,
I'm afraid you get restless.

843
00:35:19,010 --> 00:35:21,510
I'd rather have you sleep.

844
00:35:22,520 --> 00:35:25,520
- [Servo] Hey, her
hair has a navel!

845
00:35:28,020 --> 00:35:29,530
- [Mike] Ah,
they're co-gargling.

846
00:35:29,520 --> 00:35:31,020
(machine buzzing)

847
00:35:31,020 --> 00:35:32,520
- Excuse me, dear, I'm
expecting something.

848
00:35:32,530 --> 00:35:34,030
- What?

849
00:35:34,030 --> 00:35:35,030
- Watch.

850
00:35:37,030 --> 00:35:39,540
- [Crow] Hef taught
me that move.

851
00:35:41,540 --> 00:35:43,540
- The Foreign Office
today confirmed

852
00:35:43,540 --> 00:35:45,040
the upcoming official visit of

853
00:35:45,040 --> 00:35:48,040
British Finance Minister,
Sir Harold Clark.

854
00:35:48,040 --> 00:35:50,050
Sir Harold and his
charming wife, Lady Clark,

855
00:35:50,040 --> 00:35:53,040
will arrive here on
Thursday, May 5th.

856
00:35:53,050 --> 00:35:55,050
- May 5th.

857
00:35:55,050 --> 00:35:56,550
Isn't the 6th your birthday?

858
00:35:56,550 --> 00:35:59,060
- [Servo] We're going over
to the Andersons for dinner.

859
00:35:59,050 --> 00:36:01,550
- What would you
like me to give you?

860
00:36:01,560 --> 00:36:04,560
- [Mike] Hmmm,
something non-penis.

861
00:36:04,560 --> 00:36:07,060
- There must be
something I haven't got.

862
00:36:07,060 --> 00:36:09,070
- [Reporter] A reception
is planned in their honor

863
00:36:09,060 --> 00:36:11,060
in historic St. Just Castle.

864
00:36:11,060 --> 00:36:14,560
Lady Clark will wear the
famous Aksand necklace

865
00:36:14,570 --> 00:36:16,570
which is comprised
of 11 emeralds,

866
00:36:16,570 --> 00:36:19,580
the most perfect in the world.

867
00:36:19,570 --> 00:36:21,070
- Those emeralds.

868
00:36:23,080 --> 00:36:26,080
- [Servo] Typical guy,
doesn't pick up the hint.

869
00:36:26,080 --> 00:36:28,580
(mysterious jingle)

870
00:36:28,580 --> 00:36:30,090
- [Man] You've arrived.

871
00:36:30,080 --> 00:36:33,580
- [Mike] Wow, the
addition blends right in.

872
00:36:35,090 --> 00:36:36,090
- [Crow] Got tickets?

873
00:36:36,090 --> 00:36:37,090
Need two.

874
00:36:43,600 --> 00:36:46,100
- You got the time, baby?

875
00:36:46,100 --> 00:36:48,100
- Depends, handsome.

876
00:36:48,100 --> 00:36:51,610
So far I've turned
down all offers.

877
00:36:51,610 --> 00:36:53,110
- Why?

878
00:36:53,110 --> 00:36:54,110
What's your price?

879
00:36:54,110 --> 00:36:58,110
- [Servo] Are you planning
to buy me in bulk?

880
00:36:59,610 --> 00:37:01,110
- An emerald necklace.

881
00:37:01,110 --> 00:37:04,610
- [Mike] You're not gonna
give me the time, are you?

882
00:37:04,620 --> 00:37:05,620
- You look worth it.

883
00:37:05,620 --> 00:37:06,620
Hop in.

884
00:37:06,620 --> 00:37:07,620
- [Crow] "You look weathered."

885
00:37:07,620 --> 00:37:09,130
What a nice thing to say.

886
00:37:09,120 --> 00:37:10,620
- [Servo] Look out!

887
00:37:13,630 --> 00:37:15,130
- Well?

888
00:37:15,130 --> 00:37:16,630
- [Mike] A young Sam
Donaldson scores.

889
00:37:16,630 --> 00:37:18,630
- Lady Clark's room is...

890
00:37:19,630 --> 00:37:21,630
Is the highest window,
the one that's lit up.

891
00:37:21,640 --> 00:37:23,140
- And?

892
00:37:23,140 --> 00:37:24,640
- [Crow] That building
looks like us.

893
00:37:24,640 --> 00:37:27,140
- I saw a truck delivering
some television equipment.

894
00:37:27,140 --> 00:37:29,150
- Closed-circuit TV.

895
00:37:29,140 --> 00:37:30,640
- [Servo] Ali/Spinks tonight.

896
00:37:30,640 --> 00:37:32,140
- Many police?

897
00:37:32,150 --> 00:37:34,150
- About 50 outside.

898
00:37:34,150 --> 00:37:36,150
And 30 inside
dressed as waiters.

899
00:37:36,150 --> 00:37:38,650
- Hmm, and Ginko's the chef.

900
00:37:38,650 --> 00:37:39,660
- I didn't see Ginko.

901
00:37:39,650 --> 00:37:41,650
- [Mike] That squares my chin.

902
00:37:41,660 --> 00:37:44,160
- If you didn't see
him, he's there.

903
00:37:44,160 --> 00:37:45,160
- Huh?
- Huh?

904
00:37:45,160 --> 00:37:47,160
- Anyone notice you?

905
00:37:47,160 --> 00:37:48,660
- Oh, one of the
girls on the sidewalk

906
00:37:48,660 --> 00:37:50,670
asked me a few questions.

907
00:37:50,660 --> 00:37:53,660
She thought I was trying
to move in on her beat.

908
00:37:53,670 --> 00:37:56,670
- I figured Diabolik would
make a play for those emeralds.

909
00:37:56,670 --> 00:37:57,670
- Who wouldn't?

910
00:37:57,670 --> 00:37:59,180
They're beautiful!

911
00:38:00,170 --> 00:38:02,170
- Dry up, stupid!

912
00:38:02,180 --> 00:38:03,180
- (laughing) Sure.

913
00:38:03,180 --> 00:38:04,180
- [Crow] She's a sex clown.

914
00:38:04,180 --> 00:38:06,680
- This might be our big chance.

915
00:38:06,680 --> 00:38:09,690
If you're right, I'll
take care of you, sweetie.

916
00:38:09,680 --> 00:38:12,180
- Want me to describe her?

917
00:38:12,190 --> 00:38:13,190
- [Servo] Who's
straight in this scene?

918
00:38:13,190 --> 00:38:14,690
- Not to me, to Tony.

919
00:38:16,190 --> 00:38:17,690
Tell him!

920
00:38:17,690 --> 00:38:19,200
- [Mike] Time for blood
pressure check, gentlemen.

921
00:38:19,190 --> 00:38:22,190
- [Woman] Well, look at that.

922
00:38:22,200 --> 00:38:23,700
That's a funny-looking thing.

923
00:38:23,700 --> 00:38:24,700
(goofy laughter)

924
00:38:24,700 --> 00:38:25,700
What is it?

925
00:38:26,700 --> 00:38:27,700
Hey, I'm talking to you!

926
00:38:27,700 --> 00:38:29,210
What is it?

927
00:38:29,200 --> 00:38:31,700
- You'll see, and
don't touch it.

928
00:38:31,710 --> 00:38:32,710
- [Mike] Guys, he sees us!

929
00:38:32,710 --> 00:38:34,710
- Whoa, hey!
- Did she have a face...

930
00:38:34,710 --> 00:38:35,210
- Huh?

931
00:38:36,710 --> 00:38:37,710
- Like this?

932
00:38:37,710 --> 00:38:38,710
Was her face like this?

933
00:38:38,710 --> 00:38:40,220
- No, like this.

934
00:38:40,210 --> 00:38:41,710
- Okay, let's go on, her eyes?

935
00:38:41,720 --> 00:38:44,720
(mysterious music)

936
00:38:44,720 --> 00:38:46,720
- [Crow] No, no, stop
there, stop there.

937
00:38:46,720 --> 00:38:47,720
No, no, wait, go back.

938
00:38:47,720 --> 00:38:49,230
Go back.

939
00:38:49,220 --> 00:38:50,720
No, it was not like
that, what'd'ya doin'?

940
00:38:50,720 --> 00:38:52,220
No, no, that one, that one.

941
00:38:52,230 --> 00:38:52,730
D'oh!

942
00:38:55,230 --> 00:38:58,730
- [Servo] No, she wasn't Hitler!

943
00:38:58,730 --> 00:39:00,240
- [Mike] This is actually
Electric Ladyland.

944
00:39:00,230 --> 00:39:02,730
- Yeah, yeah, that's her!

945
00:39:02,740 --> 00:39:04,240
Just like real.

946
00:39:04,240 --> 00:39:07,740
- Get 5,000 copies of this
printed and circulate them.

947
00:39:07,740 --> 00:39:09,750
She will not get away!

948
00:39:10,740 --> 00:39:13,740
- [Crow] Cleopatra
drives a Jaguar.

949
00:39:17,750 --> 00:39:20,260
- Good night.
- Good night.

950
00:39:20,250 --> 00:39:22,250
- Good night, so
nice to see you.

951
00:39:22,260 --> 00:39:24,260
- [Servo] Thanks
for helping us move.

952
00:39:24,260 --> 00:39:26,260
- Good night.
- Good night.

953
00:39:27,260 --> 00:39:28,760
Good night.

954
00:39:28,760 --> 00:39:30,270
- [Mike] I finished
the magic flute.

955
00:39:30,260 --> 00:39:32,260
- Boy, glad that's over.

956
00:39:32,270 --> 00:39:33,770
- I hope it's not.

957
00:39:33,770 --> 00:39:36,770
Why do you think I gave the
necklace all that publicity?

958
00:39:36,770 --> 00:39:39,280
He'll never be able to
resist those emeralds.

959
00:39:39,270 --> 00:39:43,270
Now we'll sit back and
wait to spring the trap.

960
00:39:45,280 --> 00:39:46,780
- [Crow] Oh, can't
the Navy SEALs

961
00:39:46,780 --> 00:39:49,790
ever just come in
the front door?

962
00:39:50,780 --> 00:39:54,780
- [Servo] Wife
drops her earring...

963
00:39:54,790 --> 00:39:55,790
- [Mike] Clunk.

964
00:39:58,290 --> 00:39:59,300
- [Crow] Let's go
security guarding now,

965
00:39:59,290 --> 00:40:00,790
where everybody's learning how.

966
00:40:00,790 --> 00:40:03,790
Come on and security
guard with me!

967
00:40:07,300 --> 00:40:08,800
- [Servo] I'm a Nazi,
but I love color!

968
00:40:08,800 --> 00:40:09,810
What can I do?

969
00:40:10,800 --> 00:40:14,300
(waves splashing)

970
00:40:14,310 --> 00:40:16,810
- [Mike] I hurl my
skinniness at you!

971
00:40:16,810 --> 00:40:18,810
- [Crow] Stupid jerk!

972
00:40:22,820 --> 00:40:25,820
- [Servo] Wait, I'm
just the postman!

973
00:40:29,320 --> 00:40:32,320
- [Mike] I exfoliate
while I creep.

974
00:40:36,330 --> 00:40:38,830
- [Crow] Omaha Beach, June 5th.

975
00:40:38,830 --> 00:40:39,840
I was early.

976
00:40:45,840 --> 00:40:47,340
- [Mike] Look at that,

977
00:40:47,340 --> 00:40:50,350
he's got knives stuck
in every cranny.

978
00:40:50,340 --> 00:40:52,840
- [Servo] I'm just a neighbor!

979
00:40:55,350 --> 00:40:58,850
- [Mike] You gotta
get rid of that cyst.

980
00:41:00,850 --> 00:41:02,350
- Sir Harold...
- Are you dead?

981
00:41:02,360 --> 00:41:04,360
- If you don't mind, I'd like
to check your room again.

982
00:41:04,360 --> 00:41:05,360
- Please do.

983
00:41:05,360 --> 00:41:06,860
- How romantic.

984
00:41:06,860 --> 00:41:07,860
It makes me feel I'm living

985
00:41:07,860 --> 00:41:10,370
in the days of highway robbers.

986
00:41:10,360 --> 00:41:12,360
- [Mike] Hang on (snoring).

987
00:41:12,370 --> 00:41:13,870
- When I return to London,

988
00:41:13,870 --> 00:41:17,370
I will have such exciting
things to tell to my friends.

989
00:41:17,370 --> 00:41:19,380
- [Crow] C'mon, honey,
I want you, baby!

990
00:41:19,370 --> 00:41:20,370
Get moving!

991
00:41:23,380 --> 00:41:25,380
- [Servo] My butt is weird.

992
00:41:29,380 --> 00:41:33,380
- [Mike] Now for my
ACME Giant Pogo Stick.

993
00:41:33,390 --> 00:41:34,890
- [Crow] I hate when
the party is done

994
00:41:34,890 --> 00:41:38,390
and you just got a couple
old people left over.

995
00:41:41,390 --> 00:41:42,390
(Servo vomiting)

996
00:41:42,400 --> 00:41:43,900
- [Crow] Look out!

997
00:41:47,400 --> 00:41:48,900
- No danger on this side.

998
00:41:48,900 --> 00:41:50,910
Slippery wall straight down.

999
00:41:50,900 --> 00:41:52,900
A fly couldn't climb it.

1000
00:41:52,910 --> 00:41:55,410
Lady Clark, may I ask you
to leave your necklace

1001
00:41:55,410 --> 00:41:56,910
on this table all night?

1002
00:41:56,910 --> 00:41:59,420
Part of our security
arrangements.

1003
00:41:59,410 --> 00:42:02,410
- Why, of course, inspector,
anything you'd like.

1004
00:42:02,420 --> 00:42:04,420
- Now I wish you
both good night.

1005
00:42:04,420 --> 00:42:05,420
- Bye-bye, to you.

1006
00:42:05,420 --> 00:42:07,420
- Good night.
- Good night.

1007
00:42:07,420 --> 00:42:09,930
- [Mike] Come along, Vivaldi.

1008
00:42:11,420 --> 00:42:15,920
- [Servo] You're gonna play
the Montgolfier brothers.

1009
00:42:16,930 --> 00:42:20,440
- [Mike] Hey, he's
double-bagging himself.

1010
00:42:20,430 --> 00:42:22,930
- [Crow] Now I'm gonna put a
nice red one over this one.

1011
00:42:22,940 --> 00:42:25,440
(tense music)

1012
00:42:29,440 --> 00:42:31,440
- [Servo] Brought his Lars
Tetens cigars with him.

1013
00:42:31,440 --> 00:42:32,440
That's good.

1014
00:42:37,450 --> 00:42:39,460
- [Mike] Oh boy, this is
gonna take a long time.

1015
00:42:39,450 --> 00:42:40,450
- [Crow] Yup.

1016
00:42:41,960 --> 00:42:45,960
Ah, he's just skittering
up the wall, isn't he?

1017
00:42:47,460 --> 00:42:50,970
- [Servo] He needs
Wallace's trousers.

1018
00:42:50,960 --> 00:42:53,960
- [Mike] I'm getting
a funny feeling.

1019
00:42:56,970 --> 00:43:00,980
- [Crow] Scraping
sounds reverberate
throughout the castle.

1020
00:43:02,980 --> 00:43:05,980
(helicopter whirring)

1021
00:43:05,980 --> 00:43:06,980
- [Servo] Help?

1022
00:43:08,980 --> 00:43:10,990
