up some speakers.

1271
00:53:42,580 --> 00:53:44,090
It's gonna be great.

1272
00:53:47,090 --> 00:53:48,090
- [Servo] Bad guy.

1273
00:53:48,090 --> 00:53:51,090
- Enterprise one,
three-three-three.

1274
00:53:52,590 --> 00:53:55,100
- I saw your ad
regarding white Jaguar.

1275
00:53:55,090 --> 00:53:56,090
- [Mike] How new are the tires?

1276
00:53:56,100 --> 00:53:57,600
- What's your price?

1277
00:53:57,600 --> 00:53:59,100
- $10 million.

1278
00:54:00,100 --> 00:54:01,100
Plus...

1279
00:54:01,100 --> 00:54:02,100
- [Crow] Dealer and prep.

1280
00:54:02,100 --> 00:54:03,610
- An emerald necklace.

1281
00:54:03,600 --> 00:54:04,600
- Right.

1282
00:54:06,110 --> 00:54:08,610
- And don't try to pull any
of the funny stuff, huh?

1283
00:54:08,610 --> 00:54:11,610
I've got a couple of experts
at dealing with women here.

1284
00:54:11,610 --> 00:54:13,110
- [Servo] Dudley
Moore and Rick James.

1285
00:54:13,110 --> 00:54:14,120
- You might not find it too easy

1286
00:54:14,110 --> 00:54:16,110
to recognize her afterwards.

1287
00:54:16,120 --> 00:54:18,620
- [Mike] No, I was calling
about a white Jaguar?

1288
00:54:18,620 --> 00:54:21,620
- I accept your conditions.

1289
00:54:21,620 --> 00:54:23,120
- That's what I like to hear.

1290
00:54:23,120 --> 00:54:24,130
- [Crow] He has a
pillow top face.

1291
00:54:24,120 --> 00:54:25,120
- Yes.

1292
00:54:26,130 --> 00:54:29,630
Meet me at Sibby's at
the Break-In Airport.

1293
00:54:31,130 --> 00:54:34,140
- [Servo] He sounded nice.

1294
00:54:34,130 --> 00:54:37,130
- Get me Inspector Ginko.

1295
00:54:37,140 --> 00:54:39,140
- [Mike] Welcome, Dr. Meacham.

1296
00:54:39,140 --> 00:54:41,640
(foreboding music)

1297
00:54:41,640 --> 00:54:45,650
- [Crow] So you like my
cool conversion plane?

1298
00:54:45,640 --> 00:54:47,140
- [Servo] Ah,
they're gonna put him

1299
00:54:47,150 --> 00:54:50,650
over the trap door and
drop him three feet.

1300
00:54:52,150 --> 00:54:56,660
- [Mike] You had more than
one carry-on, you bastard.

1301
00:54:58,160 --> 00:54:59,660
- [Servo] I have a
flashing appointment.

1302
00:54:59,660 --> 00:55:01,660
Is this gonna take long?

1303
00:55:01,660 --> 00:55:03,670
(engine turning)

1304
00:55:03,660 --> 00:55:05,160
- Go check them.

1305
00:55:07,170 --> 00:55:11,170
- [Mike] It's full of Jean
Nate Friction Pour Le Bain!

1306
00:55:12,670 --> 00:55:16,680
- [Crow] We're seeing the
plane's private parts!

1307
00:55:18,680 --> 00:55:20,180
- It all seems to be here.

1308
00:55:20,180 --> 00:55:22,180
- [Servo] And I'm
a cartoon walrus!

1309
00:55:22,180 --> 00:55:23,690
- The necklace.

1310
00:55:23,680 --> 00:55:25,180
- When I've got Eva back.

1311
00:55:25,180 --> 00:55:27,180
- No necklace, no Eva.

1312
00:55:28,190 --> 00:55:30,190
That's the deal.

1313
00:55:30,190 --> 00:55:33,700
- Is that the only deal you've
got going today, Valmont?

1314
00:55:33,690 --> 00:55:35,190
- I don't have to talk.

1315
00:55:35,190 --> 00:55:36,690
- [Mike] I'd rather just cuddle.

1316
00:55:36,700 --> 00:55:38,700
I could kill you instead.

1317
00:55:40,200 --> 00:55:41,700
- Go ahead.

1318
00:55:41,700 --> 00:55:44,210
All you've got to do
is push that button.

1319
00:55:44,200 --> 00:55:49,200
- [Crow] That didn't have
the impact I'd hoped for.

1320
00:55:49,210 --> 00:55:52,710
- Valmont, this is
most unprofessional.

1321
00:55:52,710 --> 00:55:54,720
- [Henchman] Boss, we're
over the target now.

1322
00:55:54,710 --> 00:55:56,210
- [Servo] We need
any discount items?

1323
00:55:56,220 --> 00:55:57,720
- Circle this spot.

1324
00:55:57,720 --> 00:55:58,720
- [Henchman] Gotcha.

1325
00:55:58,720 --> 00:55:59,720
(intercom buzzing)

1326
00:55:59,720 --> 00:56:01,220
- [Crow] Excuse me.

1327
00:56:05,220 --> 00:56:06,720
- That's where Eva is.

1328
00:56:06,730 --> 00:56:10,230
- [Mike] Boss, you look
chilly, so I brought you this.

1329
00:56:10,230 --> 00:56:12,230
- [Valmont] Ever jumped before?

1330
00:56:12,230 --> 00:56:13,740
- [Servo] Once, from
the teeter-totter, yeah.

1331
00:56:13,730 --> 00:56:14,730
- [Valmont] Nope.

1332
00:56:14,730 --> 00:56:16,230
First, the necklace.

1333
00:56:18,240 --> 00:56:19,740
Hold it.

1334
00:56:19,740 --> 00:56:21,240
I'll take it.

1335
00:56:21,240 --> 00:56:22,240
- [Mike] Well, I
was just reaching

1336
00:56:22,240 --> 00:56:25,250
for my snotty Kleenex, but sure.

1337
00:56:25,240 --> 00:56:26,740
- [Valmont] Now.

1338
00:56:32,250 --> 00:56:34,760
- [Crow] Eww, it's all
warm from your pocket!

1339
00:56:34,750 --> 00:56:37,750
(dramatic music)

1340
00:56:38,760 --> 00:56:42,760
- [Mike] Like I quickly showed
all three of your faces?

1341
00:56:48,770 --> 00:56:51,770
- [Servo] But I'm
an evil mastermind!

1342
00:56:55,270 --> 00:56:58,770
(everyone laughing)

1343
00:56:58,780 --> 00:57:01,280
- [Mike] Ha ha ha, this is fun!

1344
00:57:03,280 --> 00:57:06,290
- [Crow] My leg is
turning one-dimensional!

1345
00:57:06,290 --> 00:57:06,790
(loud explosion)

1346
00:57:06,790 --> 00:57:08,790
- [Servo] Peanut dust!

1347
00:57:10,290 --> 00:57:12,290
- I almost forgot.

1348
00:57:12,290 --> 00:57:13,290
When I stumbled,

1349
00:57:13,290 --> 00:57:15,800
I attached a magnetic
capsule to your plane.

1350
00:57:15,790 --> 00:57:16,790
- Who cares?

1351
00:57:16,800 --> 00:57:17,800
Pull the cord!

1352
00:57:19,300 --> 00:57:20,300
Pull the cord!

1353
00:57:20,300 --> 00:57:21,800
- [Mike] No, it's
"pull the string!"

1354
00:57:21,800 --> 00:57:23,810
- I know it's a trap, Valmont!

1355
00:57:23,800 --> 00:57:25,800
Is Eva down there or only Ginko?

1356
00:57:25,800 --> 00:57:27,300
- Yeah, yeah!

1357
00:57:27,310 --> 00:57:28,810
She's there, in the cabin!

1358
00:57:28,810 --> 00:57:30,810
- And Ginko, is Ginko
down there, too?

1359
00:57:30,810 --> 00:57:32,310
- Yeah, yeah!

1360
00:57:32,310 --> 00:57:34,820
- [Crow] Like whoa, man, yeah!

1361
00:57:35,810 --> 00:57:38,810
- [Servo] Great, it's
a picnic umbrella.

1362
00:57:40,320 --> 00:57:40,820
D'oh!

1363
00:57:42,320 --> 00:57:45,330
- [Mike] Wow, I really
missed Yankee Stadium.

1364
00:57:45,320 --> 00:57:48,820
(hard thud)
(guttural groan)

1365
00:57:48,830 --> 00:57:52,330
- [Crow] Ow, I crushed
all my Pringles.

1366
00:57:53,830 --> 00:57:54,830
- It's a trap.

1367
00:57:54,830 --> 00:57:56,830
Valmont's made a
deal with Ginko.

1368
00:57:56,840 --> 00:57:58,340
Are you all right?

1369
00:57:58,340 --> 00:58:01,840
- [Servo] If my wig
is straight, I'm fine.

1370
00:58:01,840 --> 00:58:03,340
- Damn you, Ginko.

1371
00:58:05,340 --> 00:58:09,340
- [Mike] There's people
coming, I gotta straighten up.

1372
00:58:09,350 --> 00:58:10,850
- [Crow] Rat Patrol, too?

1373
00:58:10,850 --> 00:58:11,350
Man!

1374
00:58:13,850 --> 00:58:17,850
- [Servo] Oh, they're
trucking in Nittany Lions.

1375
00:58:19,360 --> 00:58:22,360
- [Crow] Is it too
windy back there?

1376
00:58:25,860 --> 00:58:29,360
- [Mike] Next birthday, I'm
taking you to Olive Garden.

1377
00:58:29,370 --> 00:58:31,370
(heavy breathing)

1378
00:58:31,370 --> 00:58:32,370
- You hide back in the cabin.

1379
00:58:32,370 --> 00:58:34,380
I'll draw their fire.

1380
00:58:34,370 --> 00:58:35,870
If they get me, you
know what to do.

1381
00:58:35,870 --> 00:58:36,870
- [Crow] Hook up with
some other idiot?

1382
00:58:36,880 --> 00:58:37,880
- But--

1383
00:58:41,380 --> 00:58:43,380
- Run, or they get us both.

1384
00:58:45,880 --> 00:58:47,380
- [Servo] Okay,
I'll go find Nova

1385
00:58:47,390 --> 00:58:49,890
and hang with her for a while.

1386
00:58:52,390 --> 00:58:54,900
(tires screeching)

1387
00:58:54,890 --> 00:58:56,390
- [Mike] Thought you guys were
gonna take the coast road.

1388
00:58:56,400 --> 00:58:57,900
Where'd you go?

1389
00:58:57,900 --> 00:58:59,400
- Inspector, we've
got him this time.

1390
00:58:59,400 --> 00:59:00,900
He's surrounded.

1391
00:59:00,900 --> 00:59:03,400
- [Crow] Ha, they don't know
about my pencil-thin arms!

1392
00:59:03,400 --> 00:59:05,410
(rhythmic primal music)

1393
00:59:05,400 --> 00:59:07,400
- [Servo] George, George,
George of the Jungle!

1394
00:59:07,410 --> 00:59:09,410
Strong as he can be.

1395
00:59:14,410 --> 00:59:15,410
- [Mike] Good job, tree.

1396
00:59:15,410 --> 00:59:16,410
Take it easy.

1397
00:59:19,420 --> 00:59:20,920
(rapid gunfire)

1398
00:59:20,920 --> 00:59:21,920
- [Crow] Ah-ha, I'll
give away my position!

1399
00:59:21,920 --> 00:59:22,920
Heh heh heh.

1400
00:59:22,920 --> 00:59:25,930
(rapid gunfire)

1401
00:59:25,920 --> 00:59:28,420
- [Servo] I was
cleaning the erasers!

1402
00:59:28,430 --> 00:59:30,930
(loud gunfire)

1403
00:59:30,930 --> 00:59:32,930
(loud gunfire)

1404
00:59:32,930 --> 00:59:34,440
(loud gunfire)

1405
00:59:34,430 --> 00:59:35,930
- [Mike] Hey, and I let
your ride on my parachute!

1406
00:59:35,930 --> 00:59:38,430
(loud gunfire)

1407
00:59:39,940 --> 00:59:43,950
- [Crow] I must remember to
have my face resharpened.

1408
00:59:43,940 --> 00:59:45,440
(ethereal music)

1409
00:59:45,440 --> 00:59:47,940
- [Servo] Damn,
I'm out of staples.

1410
00:59:47,950 --> 00:59:50,950
- I've got you, Diabolik.

1411
00:59:50,950 --> 00:59:51,950
Come on out.

1412
00:59:51,950 --> 00:59:53,450
- Valmont!

1413
00:59:53,450 --> 00:59:54,960
Don't play the hero!

1414
00:59:54,950 --> 00:59:56,450
- [Mike] Oh, Valmont
playing the hero.

1415
00:59:56,460 --> 00:59:58,960
Why does that not surprise me?

1416
00:59:59,960 --> 01:00:01,960
- [Servo] Your pacing is...

1417
01:00:01,960 --> 01:00:02,960
so...

1418
01:00:04,460 --> 01:00:05,960
important to a...

1419
01:00:06,470 --> 01:00:07,470
movie.

1420
01:00:12,970 --> 01:00:15,480
- [Crow] Eh, I'll
just try this again.

1421
01:00:15,470 --> 01:00:16,970
- [Servo] D'oh!

1422
01:00:16,980 --> 01:00:17,980
D'oh, d'oh, god,
gotta play the hero.

1423
01:00:17,980 --> 01:00:19,980
D'oh, oh, d'oh!

1424
01:00:19,980 --> 01:00:21,480
D'oh, ow!

1425
01:00:21,480 --> 01:00:23,480
(rapid gunfire)

1426
01:00:23,480 --> 01:00:23,990
- Now.

1427
01:00:29,490 --> 01:00:31,490
Diabolik!

1428
01:00:31,490 --> 01:00:31,990
Give up!

1429
01:00:32,990 --> 01:00:35,000
- [Mike] Yeah,
yeah, yeah, hang on.

1430
01:00:34,990 --> 01:00:36,990
I gotta get a Sen-Sen.

1431
01:00:39,500 --> 01:00:42,500
- [Crow] Damn
child-proof spy stuff!

1432
01:00:45,500 --> 01:00:48,500
- [Servo] My steel
reusable Fleet.

1433
01:00:50,010 --> 01:00:54,020
- [Mike] Maybe I can run real
fast and push it into him.

1434
01:00:55,510 --> 01:00:56,510
- [Crow] I wasn't
getting enough iron.

1435
01:00:56,520 --> 01:00:59,520
(mechanical click)

1436
01:01:02,020 --> 01:01:03,520
- [Servo] He swallowed
the silver thing.

1437
01:01:03,520 --> 01:01:04,030
We're sunk.

1438
01:01:08,530 --> 01:01:10,530
- [Mike] This could
be a long stand off.

1439
01:01:10,530 --> 01:01:13,030
I'd better take
care of, you know.

1440
01:01:15,030 --> 01:01:18,530
- [Crow] Uh, Spock,
are you going back?

1441
01:01:22,040 --> 01:01:26,050
- [Servo] Wonder if I can
see my backyard from up here?

1442
01:01:27,550 --> 01:01:28,550
- [Mike] Ah-ha!

1443
01:01:28,550 --> 01:01:29,550
Oh.

1444
01:01:34,050 --> 01:01:37,550
- [Servo] It's been
a hard day's night.

1445
01:01:39,060 --> 01:01:41,060
- [Crow] Diabol?

1446
01:01:41,060 --> 01:01:43,060
Diab, how you doing?

1447
01:01:45,060 --> 01:01:46,560
- [Servo] He's dead, I
have a huge forehead.

1448
01:01:46,570 --> 01:01:48,570
What else can go wrong?

1449
01:01:53,570 --> 01:01:55,580
- [Mike] Good night,
sweet thin guy.

1450
01:01:55,570 --> 01:01:59,570
- [Crow] A flight of Jaguars
sing thee to thy rest.

1451
01:02:05,580 --> 01:02:07,580
- [Servo] Oh, I suppose
he's young and has hair.

1452
01:02:07,590 --> 01:02:09,590
That means I'm just crap.

1453
01:02:10,590 --> 01:02:13,090
- [Doctor] So, this is
the famous Diabolik?

1454
01:02:13,090 --> 01:02:15,100
- [Assistant] Yes, doctor.

1455
01:02:15,090 --> 01:02:16,090
- Get him ready.

1456
01:02:16,090 --> 01:02:16,590
- Yes, sir.

1457
01:02:16,600 --> 01:02:19,600
(busy chatter)

1458
01:02:19,600 --> 01:02:20,600
- Is it true he's dead.
- Yes.

1459
01:02:20,600 --> 01:02:22,600
- Was he poisoned?

1460
01:02:22,600 --> 01:02:26,110
- Dr. Ferrara is
performing the autopsy.

1461
01:02:26,100 --> 01:02:27,600
- [Servo] I'm playing gearshift.

1462
01:02:27,610 --> 01:02:29,110
Vroom, vroom, heh heh.

1463
01:02:31,110 --> 01:02:33,110
- We'll begin with
a circular incision.

1464
01:02:33,110 --> 01:02:34,120
Scalpel.

1465
01:02:34,110 --> 01:02:36,610
(instruments jingling)

1466
01:02:36,620 --> 01:02:37,620
- [Crow] Oh, that's a scalpel?

1467
01:02:37,620 --> 01:02:39,120
Oh, I'll use that.

1468
01:02:42,120 --> 01:02:44,130
- [Mike] Ugh, let me get
that nose out of the way.

1469
01:02:44,120 --> 01:02:47,120
Just give me a
little room to work.

1470
01:02:48,630 --> 01:02:51,630
(dramatic music)

1471
01:02:51,630 --> 01:02:56,140
- [Crow] Here, I'll do
my own autopsy, thanks.

1472
01:02:56,130 --> 01:02:57,130
- [Servo] I'm not
Werner Klemperer!

1473
01:02:57,140 --> 01:02:59,140
Please don't hurt me!

1474
01:03:01,140 --> 01:03:03,140
- [Mike] You know, Quincy
wouldn't take crap like this.

1475
01:03:03,140 --> 01:03:04,650
- [Servo] Right.

1476
01:03:07,150 --> 01:03:09,150
- Krushan, doctor.

1477
01:03:09,150 --> 01:03:13,150
The Tibetan lamas have
used it for 3,000 years.

1478
01:03:13,150 --> 01:03:17,160
It brings on a
state of suspended
animation for 12 hours.

1479
01:03:17,160 --> 01:03:18,660
But if you're not
given the antidote,

1480
01:03:18,660 --> 01:03:20,660
the apparent death becomes real.

1481
01:03:20,660 --> 01:03:22,160
- [Servo] Anyway, I'll
get back on the table.

1482
01:03:22,160 --> 01:03:23,660
- How long's it been, Eva?

1483
01:03:23,660 --> 01:03:25,170
- [Crow] Well, it
shrank when you died--

1484
01:03:25,160 --> 01:03:26,160
Oh.

1485
01:03:28,670 --> 01:03:30,670
- 11 hours and 57 minutes.

1486
01:03:30,670 --> 01:03:32,170
- [Mike] Give or take 11 hours.

1487
01:03:32,170 --> 01:03:36,180
(Mystery Science
Theater 3000 theme)

1488
01:03:38,480 --> 01:03:40,480
- Sergeant.
- Lick me.

1489
01:03:40,480 --> 01:03:42,480
- This is our friend
Valmont's certificate.

1490
01:03:42,480 --> 01:03:44,990
- [Mike] He completed
Piano Book One.

1491
01:03:44,980 --> 01:03:48,480
- Cause of death, 11
machine gun shots.

1492
01:03:49,490 --> 01:03:50,490
11 emeralds.

1493
01:03:51,490 --> 01:03:51,990
- [Servo] And one pimple.

1494
01:03:51,990 --> 01:03:53,490
- 11 bullets.

1495
01:03:53,490 --> 01:03:54,500
To the morgue!

1496
01:03:54,490 --> 01:03:56,490
- [Crow] I'm really hungry.

1497
01:03:56,500 --> 01:03:59,000
- There, Ralph Valmont.

1498
01:03:59,000 --> 01:04:01,500
If you'll just sign this here,

1499
01:04:01,500 --> 01:04:03,500
here, here, and here.

1500
01:04:03,500 --> 01:04:04,510
- Four times.

1501
01:04:04,500 --> 01:04:06,000
- Four times, yes.

1502
01:04:07,510 --> 01:04:10,510
- [Mike] See,
Anonymous P. Hancock.

1503
01:04:13,010 --> 01:04:15,520
- [Crow] I'll take a
pack of Marlboros, too.

1504
01:04:15,510 --> 01:04:18,010
- He was basically a good boy.

1505
01:04:18,020 --> 01:04:20,520
Always sent money to mama.

1506
01:04:20,520 --> 01:04:22,520
- [Servo] Hang on, pig oyster.

1507
01:04:22,520 --> 01:04:24,530
- There there, buck up.

1508
01:04:24,520 --> 01:04:28,020
- [Crow] I'll see if I
have this in your size.

1509
01:04:31,030 --> 01:04:35,040
- [Mike] Mmm, the
baked beans are ready.

1510
01:04:35,030 --> 01:04:37,530
- He'll soon be home at last.

1511
01:04:38,040 --> 01:04:39,540
He's in peace now.

1512
01:04:41,040 --> 01:04:44,550
Let's see whether
he's ready yet.

1513
01:04:44,540 --> 01:04:46,040
Please.

1514
01:04:46,040 --> 01:04:48,040
- [Servo] I put some
semolina flour in him,

1515
01:04:48,050 --> 01:04:51,050
so he'll have a
nice, crispy crust.

1516
01:04:52,050 --> 01:04:53,550
- Yes, he's ready.

1517
01:04:53,550 --> 01:04:56,060
- [Crow] For some football!

1518
