but it's only got a little
cramped kitchenette.

2022
01:25:42,830 --> 01:25:43,830
It's real pink.

2023
01:25:49,340 --> 01:25:53,350
Shouldn't the Sandpipers
start singing right about now?

2024
01:25:57,350 --> 01:26:00,350
- [Crow] Well, I'm
off to the Iditarod.

2025
01:26:01,850 --> 01:26:04,860
- [Servo] What's
that stain up there?

2026
01:26:07,860 --> 01:26:11,860
- [Mike] If only he'd been
drenched in zero coupon bonds.

2027
01:26:15,870 --> 01:26:18,870
- [Crow] Oh, I know you
stabilized our economy,

2028
01:26:18,870 --> 01:26:20,870
but it's hard to accept.

2029
01:26:24,880 --> 01:26:27,380
- [Servo] We had so many
innocent people left to murder.

2030
01:26:27,380 --> 01:26:28,380
Yeah.

2031
01:26:31,380 --> 01:26:32,390
(sinister music)
- Can You move your car?

2032
01:26:32,380 --> 01:26:33,880
You parked me in.

2033
01:26:40,390 --> 01:26:42,400
- I was expecting
you, inspector.

2034
01:26:42,390 --> 01:26:43,390
- [Servo] I wasn't
expecting your expecting

2035
01:26:43,390 --> 01:26:47,390
when I expectorated your
injector, inspector.

2036
01:26:47,400 --> 01:26:50,400
- I knew you wouldn't be
able to resist seeing him.

2037
01:26:50,400 --> 01:26:51,400
- Please...

2038
01:26:51,400 --> 01:26:53,410
- [Mike] Get bent.

2039
01:26:53,400 --> 01:26:56,400
- Give me a few seconds more.

2040
01:26:56,410 --> 01:26:57,410
Alone.

2041
01:26:59,910 --> 01:27:02,420
- [Crow] Oh, man,
my nose itches.

2042
01:27:04,920 --> 01:27:06,920
- [Mike] Well, you guys
have never tricked me,

2043
01:27:06,920 --> 01:27:08,420
so I guess it's okay.

2044
01:27:09,920 --> 01:27:11,920
- [Servo] Oh, once this
giant mink gives birth to me,

2045
01:27:11,920 --> 01:27:13,930
I'll help you, honey.

2046
01:27:17,430 --> 01:27:19,430
- [Mike] Invest me wisely.

2047
01:27:24,430 --> 01:27:26,430
- [Crow] Hey, watch the hand!

2048
01:27:26,440 --> 01:27:28,940
(dramatic music)

2049
01:27:28,940 --> 01:27:33,450
- [Servo] (muffled) Woman, get
this stupid thing off of me!

2050
01:27:33,440 --> 01:27:35,440
- [Mike] Not to take
anything away from Diabolik,

2051
01:27:35,450 --> 01:27:38,450
but this guy was not the
sharpest arch-nemesis.

2052
01:27:38,450 --> 01:27:39,950
- [Crow] That's not to say
anything bad about Diabolik--

2053
01:27:39,950 --> 01:27:43,460
- [Mike] Not to take
anything away from him.

2054
01:27:43,450 --> 01:27:45,450
- Thank you, inspector.

2055
01:27:46,460 --> 01:27:48,460
You don't know
how grateful I am.

2056
01:27:48,460 --> 01:27:52,970
- [Crow] He's basically an
eyebrow delivery system.

2057
01:27:57,470 --> 01:28:01,470
- [Servo] Man, there's a cold
Heineken sitting right there!

2058
01:28:05,480 --> 01:28:06,980
♪ Deep, deep down

2059
01:28:06,980 --> 01:28:09,480
- [Mike] It doesn't really
seem like he comes out ahead.

2060
01:28:09,480 --> 01:28:09,980
- [Crow] Not really.

2061
01:28:09,980 --> 01:28:11,980
♪ Deep, deep down

2062
01:28:11,980 --> 01:28:14,490
(diabolic laughter)

2063
01:28:14,480 --> 01:28:17,480
- [Crow] Hey, who
turned off the lights?

2064
01:28:18,990 --> 01:28:23,000
- [Servo] This has been the
official biopic of Larry Fine.

2065
01:28:22,990 --> 01:28:24,990
(doors slamming)

2066
01:28:25,000 --> 01:28:27,000
(sonar beeping)

2067
01:28:27,000 --> 01:28:30,000
(doors slamming)

2068
01:28:34,000 --> 01:28:36,470
(alarm beeping)

2069
01:28:36,470 --> 01:28:37,970
- Tom, what's our situation?

2070
01:28:37,980 --> 01:28:39,480
- Beginning reentry, Mike!

2071
01:28:39,480 --> 01:28:40,480
- Good.

2072
01:28:40,480 --> 01:28:41,980
(loud explosion)
- Ugh!

2073
01:28:41,980 --> 01:28:43,480
Total heat shield failure, Mike!

2074
01:28:43,480 --> 01:28:44,980
- Bad.

2075
01:28:44,980 --> 01:28:46,490
What's going on?
- Deck Three broken away!

2076
01:28:46,480 --> 01:28:46,980
(loud explosion)

2077
01:28:46,980 --> 01:28:48,480
Deck Four broken away!

2078
01:28:48,490 --> 01:28:49,990
(loud explosion)

2079
01:28:49,990 --> 01:28:51,990
- Oh my gosh, Cambot, give
me Rocket Number Nine!

2080
01:28:51,990 --> 01:28:53,490
- Whoa, Nelly!

2081
01:28:53,490 --> 01:28:56,000
(loud explosions)
Deck Five broken away!

2082
01:28:55,990 --> 01:28:57,490
Deck Six, broken away!

2083
01:28:57,490 --> 01:28:58,490
(loud explosion)

2084
01:28:58,500 --> 01:29:00,500
Deck Seven, melting
and broken away!

2085
01:29:00,500 --> 01:29:02,000
- Gypsy, what do we do?

2086
01:29:02,000 --> 01:29:03,000
- We burn up horribly.

2087
01:29:03,000 --> 01:29:05,000
It's too dreadful
to contemplate!

2088
01:29:05,000 --> 01:29:08,510
Oh my god in heaven, please
have mercy on our souls!

2089
01:29:08,510 --> 01:29:10,010
- I'll call Pearl.

2090
01:29:10,010 --> 01:29:12,510
- Uh-oh, toxic gas filling our
lungs and our nasal passages!

2091
01:29:12,510 --> 01:29:14,010
- [Mike] Pearl!

2092
01:29:14,010 --> 01:29:15,520
- Now sing, dammit, sing!

2093
01:29:15,510 --> 01:29:20,010
♪ It's a long way
to tip a rare breed

2094
01:29:20,020 --> 01:29:23,020
♪ It's a long way

2095
01:29:24,520 --> 01:29:26,030
- Look, Nelson.

2096
01:29:26,020 --> 01:29:27,520
Move on.

2097
01:29:27,520 --> 01:29:29,020
I am.

2098
01:29:29,030 --> 01:29:31,030
(electronic static)

2099
01:29:31,030 --> 01:29:34,030
- Whoa, Deck Nine crashing
through Deck 10 and 11!

2100
01:29:34,030 --> 01:29:35,030
- This is it!

2101
01:29:35,030 --> 01:29:36,040
We're going down!

2102
01:29:36,030 --> 01:29:36,530
(loud explosion)

2103
01:29:36,530 --> 01:29:38,030
- Brace for impact!

2104
01:29:38,040 --> 01:29:40,040
- We're all gonna die!

2105
01:29:40,040 --> 01:29:42,040
- Mike, have you seen
my other sweater?

2106
01:29:42,040 --> 01:29:45,550
(panicked screaming)

2107
01:29:45,540 --> 01:29:48,540
(loud crash)

2108
01:29:48,550 --> 01:29:51,050
(loud explosion)

2109
01:29:51,050 --> 01:29:53,550
(light music)

2110
01:29:56,050 --> 01:30:00,050
- Heh heh heh, boy, oh boy,
this ConGypsCo stock is up!

2111
01:30:00,060 --> 01:30:01,560
I mean, way up!

2112
01:30:01,560 --> 01:30:04,560
- Well, Gypsy did want to let
us in on her public offering,

2113
01:30:04,560 --> 01:30:05,570
but we said no.

2114
01:30:05,560 --> 01:30:08,560
- Well, if you remember,
I made a fart noise.

2115
01:30:08,570 --> 01:30:10,570
She only took it as a no.

2116
01:30:10,570 --> 01:30:12,570
- Well, still, it
all worked out.

2117
01:30:12,570 --> 01:30:15,070
I mean, we were very fortunate
to walk away from that crash.

2118
01:30:15,070 --> 01:30:16,580
- I'll say.
- Oh, yeah.

2119
01:30:16,570 --> 01:30:17,570
- I guess if we were
all multibillionaires,

2120
01:30:17,570 --> 01:30:19,070
you guys wouldn't
have moved in with me.

2121
01:30:19,080 --> 01:30:20,580
- True.
- Yeah, that's right.

2122
01:30:20,580 --> 01:30:22,080
Sweet garden-level living.

2123
01:30:22,080 --> 01:30:25,080
One bedroom, one half-bath,
and on the bus line.

2124
01:30:25,080 --> 01:30:26,090
- Sweet!

2125
01:30:26,080 --> 01:30:27,580
- Hey, who's for rice?

2126
01:30:27,580 --> 01:30:28,580
- Would you sit down?

2127
01:30:28,590 --> 01:30:29,590
The movie's about to start!

2128
01:30:29,590 --> 01:30:31,090
- Come here, dummy!

2129
01:30:32,090 --> 01:30:34,590
- [Announcer] WTMJ TV
in Milwaukee presents

2130
01:30:34,590 --> 01:30:37,100
our Saturday afternoon
movie, The Crawling Eye.

2131
01:30:37,090 --> 01:30:40,090
(dramatic music)

2132
01:30:42,600 --> 01:30:47,110
- The Crawling Eye, the
Marty Feldman story.

2133
01:30:47,100 --> 01:30:48,600
- [Mike] Oh, Forrest Tucker.

2134
01:30:48,610 --> 01:30:52,110
He's the guy that makes sure
the trees' shirt tails are in.

2135
01:30:53,610 --> 01:30:56,120
- This movie looks kind
of familiar, doesn't it?

2136
01:30:56,110 --> 01:30:57,610
- [Servo] Hmm...

2137
01:30:58,850 --> 01:31:01,350
(MST3K Love Theme)

2138
01:32:00,910 --> 01:32:03,420
(siren whooping)

2139
01:32:03,410 --> 01:32:06,240
- [Valmont] Is that Stud coming?

